@page "/privacy"
@layout AppLayout

@* Everything on this page describes what the code does; the words are in Privacy.razor.cs and Web/PrivacyText.cs,
   which name the classes they describe, and the numbers come from the running configuration. Update it with the code. *@

<SeoHead Title="Privacy" Path="/privacy"
         Description="@(Grey ? "What TraceableAI stores, for how long, what it sends to the language model, the scholarly databases and the grey literature sites, and how it keeps the web pages a review cites. No accounts, no tracking." : "What TraceableAI stores, for how long, and what it sends to the language model and the scholarly databases. No accounts, no tracking.")" />

<DocPage Current="/privacy" Sections="DocSections" Eyebrow="Privacy" Title="What happens to your data">
    <Lead>
        There are no accounts, no advertising and no tracking. TraceableAI keeps what it needs to run your review and
            show it to you, for a limited time, and nothing else.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <div class="mt-10 rounded-card border border-line bg-page p-6 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5 text-sm">
            @foreach (var (title, text) in Summary)
            {
                <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold text-heading">@title</p>
                    <p class="text-muted mt-1">@text</p>
                </div>
            }
        </div>

        <section class="mt-10 scroll-mt-6" aria-labelledby="controller">
            <h2 id="controller" class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-heading">Who is responsible</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-ink">
                TraceableAI is run by the @Controller, Herning, Denmark. The department is the data controller for what this
                server stores. The site is a research tool and not yet an official Aarhus University website, but it follows the
                same rules as one.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-ink">
                Until the site has its own contact address, questions and requests go to the
                <a href="@ContactUrl" class="text-heading underline underline-offset-2">issues on GitHub</a>. Issues are public,
                so write only that you have a request about your data, without personal details, and you will get a private way to
                send the rest.
            </p>
        </section>

        @foreach (var (id, heading, paragraphs) in Sections.Where(x => Grey || x.Id != "web-pages"))
        {
            <section class="mt-10 scroll-mt-6" aria-labelledby="@id">
                <h2 id="@id" class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-heading">@heading</h2>
                @foreach (var paragraph in paragraphs)
                {
                    <p class="mt-4 text-ink">@paragraph</p>
                }
            </section>
        }

        <section class="mt-10 scroll-mt-6" aria-labelledby="retention">
            <h2 id="retention" class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-heading">How long things are kept</h2>
            <div class="mt-5 rounded-card border border-line bg-page overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="How long things are kept, scrolls sideways">
                <table class="w-full text-sm">
                    <caption class="sr-only">What is kept, where, and for how long</caption>
                    <thead class="bg-soft text-left text-muted">
                        <tr><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">What</th><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Where</th><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">How long</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody class="divide-y divide-line text-ink">
                        @foreach (var (what, where, howLong) in Retention)
                        {
                            <tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-medium text-heading align-top">@what</th><td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">@where</td><td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">@howLong</td></tr>
                        }
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-10 scroll-mt-6" aria-labelledby="third-parties">
            <h2 id="third-parties" class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-heading">Who else receives what</h2>
            <div class="mt-5 rounded-card border border-line bg-page overflow-hidden">
                <table class="w-full text-sm">
                    <caption class="sr-only">Services that receive data during a review</caption>
                    <thead class="bg-soft text-left text-muted">
                        <tr><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Service</th><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">What it receives</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody class="divide-y divide-line text-ink">
                        @foreach (var (service, receives) in Grey ? ThirdParties.Concat(GreyThirdParties) : ThirdParties)
                        {
                            <tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-medium text-heading align-top">@service</th><td class="px-4 py-3">@receives</td></tr>
                        }
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-4 text-ink">Mistral AI and the hosting provider handle data on the department's behalf. The search services receive only what a search needs. Each of these services has its own privacy policy. None of them receives your network address from TraceableAI; they see the server's.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-10 scroll-mt-6" aria-labelledby="rights">
            <h2 id="rights" class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-heading">Your rights</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-ink">
                Under the GDPR you can ask to see the data kept about you, to have it corrected or erased, and to restrict its use.
                You can also object to its use. There are no accounts, so the site can only find your data through the link of
                your run. Send that link with your request. You can delete a run yourself at any time.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-ink">
                The fingerprints of network addresses are not linked to a run or to anything else about you, so they cannot be
                looked up for you. They are gone after two days. If you think your data is handled wrongly, you can complain to
                <a href="@DatatilsynetUrl" class="text-heading underline underline-offset-2">Datatilsynet</a>, the Danish Data
                Protection Agency.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-10 scroll-mt-6" aria-labelledby="choices">
            <h2 id="choices" class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-heading">Your choices</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-ink">
                You can delete a run and all its files at any time from its dashboard or report page, and withdraw a report
                you added to the gallery from its report page or its gallery page. You can use your own
                Mistral key, or run TraceableAI on your own computer with a local model, so that nothing leaves your machine
                except the database searches. Questions about this page go to the
                <a href="@ContactUrl" class="text-heading underline underline-offset-2">issues on GitHub</a>.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">Last updated November 2026. The page is generated from the app's own settings, so the periods above are the ones this server uses.</p>
        </section>
    </ChildContent>
</DocPage>
